=== Analysis (QA observation, not a fix) ===
Tag colliding: "<default FloatingActionButton tag>" — the FLUTTER-ASSIGNED SENTINEL used by
ANY FloatingActionButton that does not set an explicit heroTag. This is a DIFFERENT collision
than the already-flagged regression-candidate (store_screen.dart:88 heroTag:'nothing' vs
all_items_screen.dart:96 heroTag:'nothing', reachable via Menu > All Items while Store tab
active) — that candidate's tag is the literal string 'nothing', not the default sentinel, so
this is NOT the same defect; filing as a distinct AC2 task-bug per the ticket's own instruction.
Reachable on the exact path AC2 specifies (profile-save -> back-navigation), reproduces on the
FIRST attempt from BOTH required starting tab states (Home, Store) — not a flake.

Only FABs found without an explicit heroTag in VendorApp (grep, for the engineer's fix-scoping,
NOT verified as the actual colliding pair by QA): dashboard_screen.dart:129 (always-mounted
Store-tab-jump FAB, the one demonstrated for AC1) and add_item_screen.dart:224 (AI-generator
FAB — NOT rendered in this test env since open_ai_status=0, so it cannot be the second Hero in
THIS repro). Given the AI FAB was never rendered this session, the second default-tag Hero in
this specific repro is not yet identified by QA — engineer should use Flutter DevTools' widget
inspector or a wider grep (withdraw_method_screen.dart, delivery_man_screen.dart,
coupon_screen.dart, addon_screen.dart, create_advertisement_screen.dart,
advertisement_list_screen.dart also construct FloatingActionButton without checking heroTag —
none of these were visited this QA session, so they're not implicated by observation, only by
static grep) to find the true second widget, since AppLogger.frameworkError's bounded
_frameworkStackFrameCap (8, logging-contract NEARS-1860) does not print the full Hero subtree
diagnostics needed to name it definitively.
